{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6139458","formula":"C₁₀H₆P₂S₄","hill":"C10H6P2S4","elements":["H","C","P","S"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":6.0,"P":2.0,"S":4.0},"names":{"en":"Naphthalen-1,8-diyl 1,3,2,4-dithiadiphosphetane 2,4-disulfide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Naphthalen-1,8-diyl 1,3,2,4-dithiadiphosphetane 2,4-disulfide (sometimes noted as NpP2S4) is a compound related to Lawesson's reagent formed by the reaction of 1-bromonaphthalene with P4S10, this is a 1,3,2,4-dithiadiphosphetane 2,4-disulfide which has a naphth-1,8-diyl group holding the two phosphorus atoms together. The mechanism by which the NpP2S4 forms is not yet elucidated, but it is thought to occur by a process involving free radicals, and naphthalene has been detected as a side product in its synthesis."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":11243996,"mass":316.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC2=C3C(=C1)P4(=S)SP(=S)(C3=CC=C2)S4","inchikey":"NYHOAPMWYNAQJE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2,4-bis(sulfanylidene)-3,14-dithia-2lambda5,4lambda5-diphosphatetracyclo[7.3.1.12,4.05,13]tetradeca-1(12),5,7,9(13),10-pentaene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11243996","atoms":22,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.375,"y":0.001,"z":1.508,"el":"S"},{"x":-2.375,"y":0.0,"z":-1.508,"el":"S"},{"x":-2.728,"y":-3.137,"z":0.001,"el":"S"},{"x":-2.728,"y":3.137,"z":-0.001,"el":"S"},{"x":-1.822,"y":-1.4,"z":0.0,"el":"P"},{"x":-1.822,"y":1.4,"z":0.0,"el":"P"},{"x":0.637,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.029,"y":-1.265,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.028,"y":1.265,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.06,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.721,"y":-2.453,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.722,"y":2.453,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.773,"y":-1.206,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.773,"y":1.206,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":2.109,"y":-2.424,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":2.11,"y":2.424,"z":0.001